4. macOS-15 SDK NOTE (@Observable macro / SDK pairing)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   A direct `swiftc -typecheck -sdk MacOSX15.4.sdk` of any @Observable type fails with
   "declaration name 'shouldNotifyObservers' is not covered by macro 'Observable'". Proven to be a
   toolchain/SDK pairing quirk INDEPENDENT of the surface code with a 2-line probe:
$ echo 'import Observation; @Observable final class Tiny { var n = 0 }' | swiftc -typecheck -sdk MacOSX15.4.sdk ...
   error: declaration name 'shouldNotifyObservers' is not covered by macro 'Observable'   (exit 1)
$ ... same 2 lines vs default SDK (26.5)
   (exit 0)
   The Swift 6.3 Observation macro emits a helper newer than the bundled 15.4 SDK expects. On the
   full-Xcode acceptance runner the macro + SDK are version-matched. macOS-15 compatibility is
   established by the SPM build above (platforms [.macOS(.v15)]; only APIs available since macOS
   14/15 are used). swiftc -parse of the Previews file: exit 0 (syntax valid).

